note: Words for maths. Use them in a program with:  use: maths
note: Angles are in degrees.

include: <cmath>

pi = 3.14159265358979323846, number, read only
  runs: math.pi
  web: 3.141592653589793

to sine of, given angle (a number), returning a number = std::sin({angle} * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.0)
  runs: math.sin({angle} * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.0)
  web: Math.sin({angle} * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.0)
to cosine of, given angle (a number), returning a number = std::cos({angle} * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.0)
  runs: math.cos({angle} * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.0)
  web: Math.cos({angle} * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.0)
to tangent of, given angle (a number), returning a number = std::tan({angle} * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.0)
  runs: math.tan({angle} * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.0)
  web: Math.tan({angle} * 3.14159265358979323846 / 180.0)

to round, given x (a number), returning a number = std::round({x})
  runs: (lambda a: math.copysign(math.floor(abs(a)) + (abs(a) - math.floor(abs(a)) >= 0.5), a))({x})
  web: stellanova_maths::round({x})
to round down, given x (a number), returning a number = std::floor({x})
  runs: float(math.floor({x}))
  web: Math.floor({x})
to round up, given x (a number), returning a number = std::ceil({x})
  runs: float(math.ceil({x}))
  web: Math.ceil({x})

to power of, given x (a number) and power (a number), returning a number = std::pow({x}, {power})
  runs: power_of({x}, {power})
  web: Math.pow({x}, {power})
to remainder of, given x (a number) and divided by (a number), returning a number = std::fmod({x}, {divided by})
  runs: math.fmod({x}, {divided by}) if {divided by} != 0 else math.nan
  web: (({x}) % ({divided by}))

python:
  def power_of(x, p):
      try:
          return float(math.pow(x, p))
      except (OverflowError, ValueError):
          return math.inf if x > 1 or x < -1 else math.nan

e = 2.71828182845904523536, number, read only
  runs: math.e
  web: 2.718281828459045
to logarithm of, given x (a number), returning a number = (({x}) > 0 ? std::log10({x}) : std::nan(""))
  runs: math.log10({x}) if {x} > 0 else math.nan
  web: (({x}) > 0 ? Math.log10({x}) : NaN)
to natural logarithm of, given x (a number), returning a number = (({x}) > 0 ? std::log({x}) : std::nan(""))
  runs: math.log({x}) if {x} > 0 else math.nan
  web: (({x}) > 0 ? Math.log({x}) : NaN)
to arc sine of, given x (a number), returning a number = std::asin({x}) * 180.0 / 3.14159265358979323846
  runs: math.asin({x}) * 180.0 / 3.14159265358979323846 if -1 <= {x} <= 1 else math.nan
  web: Math.asin({x}) * 180.0 / 3.14159265358979323846
to arc cosine of, given x (a number), returning a number = std::acos({x}) * 180.0 / 3.14159265358979323846
  runs: math.acos({x}) * 180.0 / 3.14159265358979323846 if -1 <= {x} <= 1 else math.nan
  web: Math.acos({x}) * 180.0 / 3.14159265358979323846
to arc tangent of, given x (a number), returning a number = std::atan({x}) * 180.0 / 3.14159265358979323846
  runs: math.atan({x}) * 180.0 / 3.14159265358979323846
  web: Math.atan({x}) * 180.0 / 3.14159265358979323846
to whole part of, given x (a number), returning a number = std::trunc({x})
  runs: float(math.trunc({x})) if math.isfinite({x}) else {x}
  web: Math.trunc({x})

javascript:
  const stellanova_maths = {
    round: (x) => Math.sign(x) * Math.round(Math.abs(x)),  // halves go away from zero, as C++ does
  };
